# Speech format for the prompter

The prompter (`Mod+Alt+S` in prompter mode) always reads `~/Videos/speech.md`.
Copy this file there and write your own speech. `Mod+Alt+R` rereads it without closing the window.

Only lines starting with `>` reach the screen. Everything else is yours: plans, links, drafts.
If the file has a `## Сценарий` section, only that section is read, up to the next `## ` heading.
Without one, the whole file is read.

## Сценарий

### Intro

> *[A heading of three hashes names a block: it shows above the current phrase with its number.]*

> A plain quote line is direct speech, in yellow; the current phrase is bold.

> Wrap a word in double asterisks to **stress** it while you speak.

> `Backticks` are dropped, so code names read as plain words.

### Demo

> *(Parentheses in italics are an action: open a file, switch a window. Bold cyan, stepped like speech.)*

> *[Square brackets in italics are a note: a topic, a pause. Grey, shown ahead, skipped when stepping.]*

> One phrase per line: `Mod+Alt+Down` goes to the next one, `Mod+Alt+Up` back.

## After the section

> This line is past the section, so the prompter never shows it.
